     "value": "Proteolytically cleaved at the tripeptide Xaa-Pro-Gln, where Xaa in the P(3) position is mostly lysine. The endoprotease may be of microbial origin. Pyroglutamate formation found on at least Gln-46, Gln-48, Gln-67, Gln-88; Gln-90; Gln-193; Gln-288 Gln-214 and Gln-295, preferentially in diabetic, and head and neck cancer patients"
